WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.234
Donald Trump

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.269
hush money and a potential indictment

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:05.038
that could be coming soon.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.106
The New York Times is reporting

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.207
that the district attorney's office

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:07.474
here in

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.942
Manhattan is signaling

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.076
Trump will likely face

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.812
criminal charges over hush money payments

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:15.281
to the adult film actress Stormy Daniels.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.117
But this is not a slam dunk.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.052
The case could pose a big challenge

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.253
for prosecutors

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.254
The Times reports

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.455
the former president was told

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:23.390
that he could appear

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.492
before a Manhattan grand jury next week

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:26.793
if he wishes to testify,

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:27.994
a strong indication

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.295
that an indictment could soon

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.698
follow Trump has repeatedly denied

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.466
having an affair with Stormy Daniels,

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.235
and he denies telling his longtime

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.603
fixer, Michael Cohen,

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:39.472
to buy her silence for $130,000.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.341
Right before the 2016

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.976
presidential election.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.110
But Cohen insists

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.146
that he has the receipts, personal checks

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:48.214
signed by the former president

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.582
to reimburse him.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:50.850
Our senior legal affairs

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:51.918
correspondent is Paula.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:52.819
She's following the story

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.054
for us this morning in Washington.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:54.721
Good morning to you.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.655
The D.A.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.991
is giving Trump the chance to testify.

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.193
Do you think he'll take it?

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:01.561
I do not.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.063
Don, we know that his lawyers

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:03.797
have recently met

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:04.831
with the district attorney

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:05.698
and they're concerned

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.233
because we're seeing this uptick

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.302
in activity in this investigation.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.470
This probe has been going on

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.838
for about five years.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:12.839
But in recent weeks, we've

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.041
suddenly seen this parade of high profile

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:15.909
witnesses, close

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.343
associates of the former president

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.279
like Kellyanne Conway and Hope Hicks.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.714
Going to testify before this grand jury?

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.450
I do not think it is likely

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.384
that the former president

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.252
will join that parade of witnesses going

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.420
before the grand jury.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.788
And a statement last night

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.557
a spokesperson for the former president

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:31.524
dismissed this whole thing

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.093
as, quote, insane.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.828
But the fact that the invitation

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:36.362
has been extended

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.931
signals that this investigation

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.332
is likely wrapping up

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.367
and that an indictment is possible.

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.437
So, Paula,

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.005
this is obviously a major development,

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.174
but it's a complicated legal theory

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:49.375
that the Manhattan attorney

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.710
is trying to apply here.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.544
There are a lot of lot

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.412
hinges on Trump's

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.414
former attorney, Michael Cohen,

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:55.515
who has been convicted.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.050
Right. And has served time.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.185
So is it a strong case

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:01.588
and is anyone even know at this point?

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:03.356
Look, we know a lot about this, right?

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:04.657
Because this case has been out there

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:05.425
for years.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:06.025
Some people,

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:07.627
some of these have been investigated

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.761
some have been charged.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.396
So we do know a lot of the basic facts

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.097
of this case.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.332
Look, Don, it's a fact.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.600
This conduct is approximately

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.802
seven years old at the court.

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.570
This is a paperwork crime

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.872
that would have to be prosecuted

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:20.540
on a pretty novel

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.208
legal theory in New York.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.610
And the witness at the center of all

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.111
this is Michael Cohen.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:25.445
And, Don,

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.813
you know, you've interviewed Cohen.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:28.014
You've spoken with him

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:30.183
every time he speaks in public.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.317
The issue of the former

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.352
president comes up

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.754
and he appears pretty arguably fixated

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:35.588
on former

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:36.389
President Trump

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.091
being charged in any good defense

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.492
attorney would seize on that

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.694
and the fact that he is a convicted liar

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.630
to try to undermine his credibility.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.698
And you really need a credible witness

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.734
to support a case like this.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.068
So the larger question is, well,

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.637
why is the district attorney

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.005
digging back into this?

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.439
Now, we know that he's

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.308
under a lot of political pressure.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.309
It's always possible

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:57.710
that they have unearthed

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:58.811
some additional evidence.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.813
But based on what we know now,

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.183
this is not the strongest case

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.651
that the former president

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:05.385
is possibly

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.553
facing as compared

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:07.153
to something

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.421
like down in Georgia,

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:09.355
where they're looking in

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.890
to his efforts to interfere

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.158
with the election outcome there.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.293
You have multiple witnesses.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.428
You have recordings, you have documents,

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:16.629
something like that.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:17.697
Even though former president's

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:18.665
attorneys will admit

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:21.000
they are much more concerned about that.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.202
But he did go to jail

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.870
for actually brokering this deal.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.772
You see, when he went here,

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.674
he had a lot of legal problems,

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.808
personal legal problems

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.843
with the IRS, with his business dealings

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.946
beyond just this hush money payment.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:33.913
And I think intelligent minds

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:34.981
can disagree

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.716
whether the National Enquirer right.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.384
Did not get enough accountability

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.085
for this.

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:40.220
But again,

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.988
at this point, it's just about the case

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.223
against the former president.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:45.358
And it is not terribly strong

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:46.593
based on the facts that we know.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.595
But, of course, we don't know everything.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:50.263
Right on. Thank you, Paula.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:51.698
Can we talk about this

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:52.765
possible indictment?

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:53.533
Not a slam dunk.

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:54.367
Everyone's like, is it coming?

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:54.801
Is it coming?

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.202
We don't know for sure.

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:57.036
But that's what they said.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.504
The winds are heading that way.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.873
What's your what's your response to this?

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.275
You know, not not a lawyer.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:03.576
This is probably the case

00:04:03.576 --> 00:04:05.445
that Trump's least afraid of

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.380
of the plethora of lawsuits,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.581
of different investigations

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.382
he's facing to

00:04:09.382 --> 00:04:10.817
within the Department of Justice.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:11.651
The Eugene Carroll

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.453
case, the Fulton County case.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.220
This is one

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.054
that they're

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.556
Trumpworld is prepared to hit back

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:17.257
if it goes the way

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.292
that we're anticipating to say this is

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:20.493
this is the liberals

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.562
still trying to undo the 2016 election

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.030
this is seven years ago.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.132
This is a weak campaign finance case.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.033
So I don't know that

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.835
I think this is some kind of a slam dunk.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:30.737
My other caution is this Trump's

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:31.671
usually emboldened

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.640
when he looks like he's under attack

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.908
as we saw after the Mar a Lago raid.

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:37.610
Even really mainstream Republicans

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.512
the Dan Crenshaw is the Marco Rubio.

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:41.214
Rubio kind of rallied around

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:42.215
Donald Trump saying

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.216
this is unprecedented.

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.951
This is an overstep of justice.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.552
I anticipate you may see this.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.321
They said he wasn't going to run until.

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.489
I don't know if that's true.

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:49.956
But remember,

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.190
they said he wasn't going to run

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.558
until that raid happened

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:53.960
and then this sort of emboldened

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.229
him, like, I'm going to definitely do it

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:57.630
emboldens his base because he

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.731
he positions himself.

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.333
You know, I am your retribution.

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.501
I am taking these fears

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:02.669
and arrows for you.

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.671
I think it honestly may help him Doesn't

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:06.105
mean justice shouldn't be served,

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.006
but something like

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:08.074
this is hardly going to be

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:08.908
Trump's undoing.

